27c5e-1b21-5014-af08-41ccb1867f6e", "stem": "For f(x)=(2x+1)/(x²−16), which statements are true? I. Its graph passes through the origin. II. It has no asymptotes. III. It is a polynomial of degree 3.", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "I only"}, {"key": "B", "text": "II only"}, {"key": "C", "text": "I and II"}, {"key": "D", "text": "None of them"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "D", "explanation": "f(0)=−1/16, so I is false. The numerator is nonzero at x=±4, giving vertical asymptotes there; y=0 is a horizontal asymptote, so II is false. This is a rational function, not a polynomial of degree 3, so III is false.", "topic": "Functions, Transformations & Graphs", "note": "Clarified the intended polynomial-degree statement; removed the unrelated data-list fragment.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 115, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:HOA 199", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "0285a55c-3fc7-5340-b55a-1916039afada", "stem": "Before discounts, pants cost $20 with 3% off, a jacket costs $44 with 4% off, a hat costs $2 with 0.2% off, and a blouse costs $23 with 1% off. What is the unrounded total for 1 hat, 1 pair of pants, 2 blouses, and 1 jacket?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "$123.99"}, {"key": "B", "text": "$100.77"}, {"key": "C", "text": "$239.90"}, {"key": "D", "text": "$109.176"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "D", "explanation": "The discounted costs are 20·0.97=19.4, 44·0.96=42.24, 2·0.998=1.996, and 2·23·0.99=45.54. Their sum is 109.176 dollars (109.18 if rounded to cents).", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Restored the whole table and specified unrounded total. Separate Q12 x³(1/x+3)=−x has no real solution: x≠0 and 3x²+x+1 has discriminant −11. Its request for a negative root is defective and remains excluded.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 116, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:HOA 200", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "6078ff2a-7f78-5a6e-a9ec-6e6cee1115c0", "stem": "What is \\([(-1/8)^2\\div(-1/4)^3]^{-1}\\)?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "1"}, {"key": "B", "text": "−1"}, {"key": "C", "text": "4"}, {"key": "D", "text": "−2"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "B", "explanation": "The squared term is 1/64 and the cubed term is −1/64. Their quotient is −1; its reciprocal is also −1.", "topic": "Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities", "note": "Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 117, "extra_sources": []}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
