. Hence EC=20.8.", "topic": "Coordinate Geometry & Circles", "note": "Transcribed the segment incidences from the original figure.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 171, "extra_sources": [], "parts": [{"label": "Q38", "question_id": "24701a15-261d-5972-81ad-1c4524bcd85a", "stem": "A model starts with 12000 tourists in 1990 and decreases by 10% annually. How many more tourists does it predict in 1993 than in 2000? Round the difference to the nearest whole number.", "choices": [], "type": "grid_in", "correct": "4564", "explanation": "The two predictions are 12000·0.9³ and 12000·0.9¹⁰. Their difference is 4563.8587188, which rounds to 4564.", "topic": "Functions, Transformations & Graphs", "note": "Split from the original shared crop; original PDF visually checked and solution independently verified."}]}, {"id": "clean:PSD 034", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "needs_source_reconstruction", "note": "The composition fragment supplies g(x)=−3x+5 but no f, so f(g(−2))=f(11) cannot be evaluated. The separate Joanne fragment supplies only her occupation, with no actual question or pay data. Both remain unpublished.", "correct": null}, {"id": "clean:PSD 038", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "df44edc0-5b98-5ca0-9ac5-e3b4deaf6c4f", "stem": "In a stated enrollment of 3636 students, the female-to-male ratio is 11:25. How many male students are there?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "2544"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2525"}, {"key": "C", "text": "2000"}, {"key": "D", "text": "1604"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "B", "explanation": "There are 11+25=36 ratio parts. Each represents 3636/36=101 students. The male count is 25·101=2525.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Removed nonessential historical claims. The preceding cubic fragment lacks its requested quantity and remains excluded.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 175, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 039", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "1c473be9-f3ea-5e49-8349-5776d6cc9dfe", "stem": "A magazine charges $15 per month plus $0.30 per premium article. What is the monthly cost for x premium articles?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "15x+0.3"}, {"key": "B", "text": "15+0.3x"}, {"key": "C", "text": "15·30+0.3x"}, {"key": "D", "text": "15·30x+0.3"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "B", "explanation": "The fixed monthly fee is 15, and the variable charge is 0.3x. Add them to obtain 15+0.3x.", "topic": "Functions, Transformations & Graphs", "note": "The preceding fourth-degree equation has no visible requested quantity and remains excluded.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 176, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 040", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "9972d402-d754-56ea-b872-05703d141e4b", "stem": "A table gives annual average prices of $1771.90, $1393.34, $1268.93, $1251.92, and $1158.86 for 2020 through 2016. What is their mean?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "$1137.20"}, {"key": "B", "text": "$1351.82"}, {"key": "C", "text": "$1368.99"}, {"key": "D", "text": "$1622.18"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "C", "explanation": "The five values sum to 6844.95. Dividing by 5 gives 1368.99.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Transcribed exactly the five most recent rows of the source table.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 177, "extra_sources": []}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
