Data Analysis", "note": "Made equal section areas and independent spins explicit."}]}, {"id": "clean:PSD 085", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "f182daf8-c908-5155-ba3b-2e51d83f32f2", "stem": "Each worker earns $800 plus commission on the same company profit: employee 2%, senior supervisor 4%, trainee 1%. Their combined monthly pay is $13650. What is the trainee’s pay, rounded to the nearest dollar?", "choices": [], "type": "grid_in", "correct": "2407", "explanation": "Combined fixed pay is 3·800=2400, leaving 11250 in commission at a combined rate of 7%. Profit is 11250/0.07. Trainee pay is 800+0.01(11250/0.07)=2407.142857…, which rounds to 2407.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Recovered the full commission table and fixed salary from page 212.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 213, "extra_sources": [], "parts": [{"label": "Q37", "question_id": "762ade0c-5d5a-54a5-9337-8da2559d2d32", "stem": "A supervisor earns $800 plus 3% of company profit. If January profit is $7000, what is the supervisor’s January pay?", "choices": [], "type": "grid_in", "correct": "1010", "explanation": "The commission is 0.03·7000=210. Adding the fixed salary gives 800+210=1010.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Restored the supervisor’s pay terms from the preceding shared table."}]}, {"id": "clean:PSD 086", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "c4eb0475-1dd6-50cf-a207-4a71f9888540", "stem": "For a 500 km trip, four taxis charge a fixed fee plus a rate per 25 km: A, 160+15 per 25 km; B, 210+13; C, 185+14; D, 150+16 (all EGP). Which is cheapest?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "Taxi A"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Taxi B"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Taxi C"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Taxi D"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "A", "explanation": "There are 500/25=20 units. The fares are A=160+300=460, B=210+260=470, C=185+280=465, and D=150+320=470. The minimum is A.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 214, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 089", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "8d38b634-5ba4-5fb6-83be-b9d2eb36e7b4", "stem": "Amir’s daily walking distances are 1678,2091,1245,1566,2100,1989,1888 m. What is their mean, rounded to the nearest tenth?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "2511.4"}, {"key": "B", "text": "1888"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1793.9"}, {"key": "D", "text": "1672.5"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "C", "explanation": "The seven distances sum to 12557 m. Their mean is 12557/7≈1793.8571 m, which rounds to 1793.9.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 216, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 090", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "e423ff81-1727-5156-ab42-76091d0bbed9", "stem": "Amir walks 1245 m on April 3 and 2100 m on April 5. What is the percentage increase, rounded to the nearest percent?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "34%"}, {"key": "B", "text": "60%"}, {"key": "C", "text": "67%"}, {"key": "D", "text": "69%"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "D", "explanation": "The increase is 855 m. Relative to the original 1245 m, this is 855/1245·100≈68.6747%, rounding to 69%.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Restored the required distances from the shared table on page 216.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 217, "extra_sources": []}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
