7-b8e2-0afd862179b8", "stem": "What is the arithmetic mean of 2¹¹ and 2²³?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "2¹⁷"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2¹⁵"}, {"key": "C", "text": "2¹⁰+2²²"}, {"key": "D", "text": "2³⁴"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "C", "explanation": "Their mean is (2¹¹+2²³)/2=2¹⁰+2²². Exponents cannot be averaged to find an arithmetic mean.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 235, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 116", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "228848f3-1aeb-53db-8603-eb07ce77b3e0", "stem": "A test has score frequencies: 40, 2 students; 55, 4; 75, 6; 80, 7; 95, 1. How many students score at least 55?", "choices": [], "type": "grid_in", "correct": "18", "explanation": "Include the groups scoring 55,75,80,95: 4+6+7+1=18 students.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Recovered the complete chart on page 235; equality at 55 is included.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 236, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 117", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "8d00a928-be66-5668-95c6-2662d9d9ee8b", "stem": "Cost is C(x)=x³/3−15x²+2000x and profit is P(x)=−x³/3+(79/3)x²+1500x. If P=R−C, what is revenue R(x)?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "(64/3)x²+3500x"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(34/3)x²+3500x"}, {"key": "C", "text": "−(2/3)x³+(64/3)x²+3500x"}, {"key": "D", "text": "−(2/3)x³+(124/3)x²−500x"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "B", "explanation": "Rearrange R=P+C. The cubic terms cancel. The quadratic coefficient is 79/3−15=(79−45)/3=34/3, and the linear coefficient is 3500.", "topic": "Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities", "note": "Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 236, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 118", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "622ef0b8-2274-5433-abb1-d3c14e98cb40", "stem": "Given f=m(v_f−v_i)/t, with m and t nonzero, solve for v_i.", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "v_i=v_f−ft/m"}, {"key": "B", "text": "v_i=v_f+ft/m"}, {"key": "C", "text": "v_i=v_f−fm/t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "v_i=v_f+fm/t"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "A", "explanation": "Multiply by t/m to get ft/m=v_f−v_i. Rearranging gives v_i=v_f−ft/m.", "topic": "Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities", "note": "Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 237, "extra_sources": []}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
