y": "B", "text": "II only"}, {"key": "C", "text": "I and II only"}, {"key": "D", "text": "I, II, and III"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "B", "explanation": "At x=3 the model gives 2.93·3+1.21=10, so II is true. A fitted prediction does not bound every actual score or guarantee an outcome, and the class mean is not supplied. Hence I and III are unjustified.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Restored the missing equals sign and replaced the unsupported deterministic “minimum required” wording in II with a model prediction.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 280, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 190", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "74015a7d-7081-51b1-9e9f-222546b94ad2", "stem": "One worker works a times as fast as each helper and completes a job in h hours. How many hours do w helpers need together, assuming positive constant rates that add?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "ahw"}, {"key": "B", "text": "hw/a"}, {"key": "C", "text": "aw/h"}, {"key": "D", "text": "ah/w"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "D", "explanation": "The worker’s rate is 1/h job per hour. Each helper’s rate is 1/(ah), so w helpers work at w/(ah). Their completion time is the reciprocal, ah/w.", "topic": "Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities", "note": "Recovered the missing B/C/D continuation from HOA 216 on page 128.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 282, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 191", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "needs_source_repair", "note": "The text states AD=BC=CD, which directly gives AD/BC=1, absent from the options. For distinct interior points it is also geometrically inconsistent. The likely intended AB=BC=CD would give 3, but that is a different premise and cannot be treated as verified without a corrected original.", "correct": "1 as printed; 3 only after changing AD to AB"}, {"id": "clean:PSD 193", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "164fc3d7-d3d1-586d-b7eb-b254d9b78988", "stem": "A payroll table lists total salaries: workers $550000, supervisors $120000, managers $36000. What percent of the total payroll goes to supervisors, rounded to the nearest percent?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "15%"}, {"key": "B", "text": "16%"}, {"key": "C", "text": "17%"}, {"key": "D", "text": "18%"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "C", "explanation": "Total payroll is 706000. Supervisors’ share is 120000/706000·100≈16.9972%, which rounds to 17%.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Restored the shared table from page 284 and its thousands-of-dollars units.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 285, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 194", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "80905e09-c6c8-5876-b1e9-94e4bbcfd21d", "stem": "A company has 400 workers sharing $550000 in salaries, 15 supervisors sharing $120000, and 3 managers sharing $36000. What is the overall mean salary, rounded to the nearest dollar?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "$1689"}, {"key": "B", "text": "$4725"}, {"key": "C", "text": "$1375"}, {"key": "D", "text": "$592"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "A", "explanation": "The total payroll is 706000 and the employee count is 400+15+3=418. Their mean is 706000/418≈1688.9952, which rounds to $1689.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 285, "extra_sources": []}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
  SELECT * INTO s FROM public.est_source_review WHERE id=v->>'id' FOR UPDATE;
