reas/independent spins explicitly. Used numeric response because D is clipped."}]}, {"id": "clean:PSD 224", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "8ec4e722-b351-57b1-a3f2-de61e1d2988b", "stem": "One card is chosen uniformly from a standard 52-card deck containing 4 jacks. What is the probability of a jack?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "1/26"}, {"key": "B", "text": "1/13"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1/4"}, {"key": "D", "text": "1/52"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "B", "explanation": "There are 4 favorable cards among 52, so the probability is 4/52=1/13.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Removed the false source claim that each suit contains only four cards.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 305, "extra_sources": []}, {"id": "clean:PSD 225", "old_status": "ocr_screened_not_verified", "status": "ready", "question_id": "c1931a34-b1f1-5169-8553-99b5847c0be5", "stem": "One card is chosen uniformly from a full standard 52-card deck. What is the probability it is a spade?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "1/13"}, {"key": "B", "text": "1/17"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1/4"}, {"key": "D", "text": "1/26"}], "type": "mcq", "correct": "C", "explanation": "A standard deck has 13 spades among 52 cards. Thus the probability is 13/52=1/4.", "topic": "Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis", "note": "Clarified a single draw from a full deck; “without replacement” does not change the probability of that first draw.", "source_document": "Math_Question_Bank_Ghoneem_Clean.pdf", "source_page": 306, "extra_sources": []}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
